STEP 5 — Database connection test

What I did:
- Created test/test_db.py. It imports the backend connection module,
  opens a connection to the local MySQL database "inspektorati", closes it,
  and prints "DB OK" if everything worked (or "DB FAILED: ..." with the
  reason if not).

How to run it:
    backend\venv\Scripts\python.exe test\test_db.py

Result:
    DB OK

Meaning:
- MySQL is running on 127.0.0.1:3306, the root login worked, and the
  database "inspektorati" exists. The backend can talk to the database.
